# Container Budget

## Context

The compose stack is **14 services**: postgres, pgbouncer, postgrest,
redis, rabbitmq, backend, celery_worker, loki, prometheus, tempo,
grafana, alloy, plus nginx and frontend from the master compose.
Langfuse / ClickHouse / MinIO / Citus workers / Redis Sentinel were
removed — LLM traces go to LangSmith (no local container).

## Hard rules

- Any new service added to a compose file comes with a one-line
  justification, in the same commit, for why an existing service
  (Redis, RabbitMQ, Postgres) can't absorb the responsibility instead.
- A2A service exposure does not default to a new container. Wire it into
  the existing `backend` FastAPI service (same app, new route/mount)
  unless there's a concrete reason — process isolation, differing
  scaling needs — that Titus has explicitly signed off on.
- Pin image tags. Do not add `:latest` — floating tags have taken this
  stack down when upstream rebuilt (RabbitMQ alpine/vfs, ClickHouse).
- No new service ships without that justification and sign-off.
